    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2XXKDQ5Dp5crxRdWfcttAXb)_\n\nNew module `sp-merge-pick` (`libraries/modules/prog/`, doc in `docs/tangles/prog/sp-merge-pick.org`, which tangles to the module byte for byte).\n\n**Flow**\n1. `C-x C-SPC g m` opens a graph log of all branches (unicode lane glyphs, Magit's colours). In the yadm repo start from `M-x yadm`.\n2. `C-c v i` marks the commit at point as INTO, `C-c v f` another as FROM. Both lines are highlighted and labelled.\n3. `C-c v p` previews the merge in memory with `git merge-tree --write-tree` and lists conflicting files; `RET` on one opens a three-way Ediff (INTO, FROM, merge base). `C-c v d` shows what FROM adds, `C-c v e` picks any file for the same Ediff.\n4. `C-c v n` starts a `--no-commit` merge (after asking, and after offering to check out INTO's branch if the worktree is clean). Then resolve with Magit `e`, Smerge or `M`, commit with `c c`, or abort with `m a`.\n\nOnly step 4 changes the worktree. Nothing commits.\n\n**Wiring**: module added to the late list in `init.el`; `sp-keys` autoloads `sp-merge-pick-log` on `m` in `lem+vc-keys` (code and doc); `load-order.org` lists the module; CHANGELOG set \"Reviewing merges in Magit\".\n\n**Tested** in headless Emacs 29.3 with Magit from Oct 2026 on a small repo with a conflict: log buffer, marks and overlays, glyph display properties, the preview and conflict list, the file buffers handed to Ediff (Ediff call stubbed), the no-commit merge including checking out INTO's branch, and the byte-compile (clean).\n\n**Not tested**: the Ediff session itself, colours and glyph widths in a real GUI or TTY, `C-c v` on the yadm repo, git older than 2.38 (the preview needs it). `docs/load-order-modules.svg` is not redrawn.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01YTUtXtp73PkpJxDVV4PBjV)_",
